	List File:	d:\code\Microcomputer_Principles\asem5113\BLINK.lst



 Line  I  Addr  Code            Source

    1:				;                  Test Program for BOOT-51
    2:				;                  ========================
    3:				;                  W.W. Heinz,  25. 6. 2002
    4:				;
    5:				; This program simply toggles the logic level of the port pin LEDPIN
    6:				; every second (12 MHz) to verify, whether all components of the chain
    7:				; assembly -> serial interface -> target system <-> bootstrap program
    8:				; are working together correctly.
    9:				; It can be adapted to your requirements with little efforts:
   10:				;
   11:				; 1. If your target system carries a LED that can be switched with a
   12:				;    bit-addressable port pin, please change the BIT symbol LEDPIN
   13:				;    accordingly. Then the program will make the LED blink.
   14:				;
   15:				;    If your LED can only be switched with a non-bit-addressable
   16:				;    port pin (say bit 2 of a port P6), simply replace the statement
   17:				;    "CPL LEDPIN" by "XRL P6,#00000100B" or something like that.
   18:				;
   19:				; 2. Change the program start address START to the location, where
   20:				;    user programs are usually loaded on your target system.
   21:				;    The program code itself is position-independent!
   22:				;
   23:				; If there is no LED on your target system, connect the port pin LEDPIN
   24:				; to a volt-meter. This may also do. Aside of P0 and P2 you may use every
   25:				; port with LEDs or spare outputs.
   26:
   27:		B	 B5	        LEDPIN BIT P3.5  ;your favorite port pin (LED preferred)
   28:
   29:		N      8000	        START CODE 8000H ;start address of user programs
   30:
   31:		N      0008	        TIME EQU 8       ;time constant in units of 250 ms (for 12 MHz)
   32:
   33:		C      8000	        ORG START        ;program start address
   34:
   35:	  8000	B2 B5		BLINK:  CPL LEDPIN       ;toggle pin  (Great, if connected to a LED!)
   36:	  8002	7B 08		        MOV R3,#TIME     ;wait for  TIME * 125 ms  (12 MHz)
   37:	  8004	7A 00		        MOV R2,#0
   38:	  8006	79 00		        MOV R1,#0
   39:	  8008	D9 FE		LOOP:   DJNZ R1,LOOP
   40:	  800A	DA FC		        DJNZ R2,LOOP
   41:	  800C	DB FA		        DJNZ R3,LOOP
   42:	  800E	80 F0		        SJMP BLINK       ;This is repeated forever,
   43:				                         ;if you don't press reset ...

